# #5833, C1. An append carrying a generation above the loaded one claims it, as #5835's
# cold path did: each key-moving close's raise becomes a shard-wide re-claim at the
# partition's next write, fencing every in-flight lower-generation write of the shard.
MODULE: ReclaimCostBoundPreArmHigherGenerationClaims
TARGET: ReclaimCostBound
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a PreArm append carrying a higher generation claims it
PERTURBS: PreArmAlloc
BOUNDS: WithKeyMove = TRUE, MaxWindows = 0, WithMixedVersion = FALSE

--- FIND
    /\ UNCHANGED <<seenP, startHead, evStart, evFloor, moveVars>>

(* OwnAllocUnstamped(a)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a higher carried generation is claimed.
    /\ gL' = gD
    /\ strayReclaims' = IF gD > gL THEN strayReclaims + 1 ELSE strayReclaims
    /\ UNCHANGED <<seenP, startHead, evStart, evFloor, gD, pend, pendGen, moved, otherMoved, dUsed, reclaims>>

(* OwnAllocUnstamped(a)
--- END
